nvidia-kmod-open (615.71.09-2+stereo3d4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Build from a source package: NVIDIA's DKMS tree of 615.71.09-2 as the
    upstream tarball and our eight patches as the quilt series, the same
    tree +stereo3d3 shipped (+stereo3d1 to +stereo3d3 repacked NVIDIA's
    binary package with the patches applied).
  * New binary package sparky-stereo-nvidia-driver-lock, required by
    nvidia-kernel-open-dkms-stereo3d: an APT preferences file generated from
    this version that keeps every NVIDIA driver package at 615.71.09-2
    (priority 1005, any other version 100) and never installs NVIDIA's or
    Debian's own NVIDIA kernel module packages (-1). A newer driver in
    NVIDIA's CUDA repository can no longer replace the HDMI 3D module or
    mismatch its userspace; CUDA toolkit packages keep updating. The lock
    package itself always follows the edition's repository (1001).
  * The NVIDIA versions in the control fields come from this changelog.

